            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0377" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/512: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-28T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                                1927—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 28—6:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>273. Following telegram has been sent to American consul general, Hankow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 28, 7 p.m. Legation has today addressed following communication to
                            all American missions, companies and individuals in all districts of
                            northern Honan south of Yellow River: ‘In view of the present civil
                            warfare Legation earnestly advises all American citizens to withdraw
                            from all districts of Honan south of Yellow River.’”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
